WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.036
-Our first guest tonight is a
Tony and Academy Award-winning

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:06.072
actress you know from movies
such as "Chicago," "Traffic,"

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:07.373
and the Netflix series
"Wednesday."

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:10.143
She stars in "National Treasure:
Edge of History,"

00:00:10.143 --> 00:00:12.444
which beings streaming
with a two-episode premier

00:00:12.444 --> 00:00:14.647
December 14th on Disney+.

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:15.682
Let's take a look.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:18.618
-Finding anything you like?

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:21.587 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:23.089
-You're Billie?

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:25.425
-Who were you expecting?
-I don't know.

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:27.260
But I didn't expect someone who
looks like

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.495
they walked out of the town
in "Big Little Lies."

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:31.364
-This isn't a television show.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.699
Where's the relic?

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:34.667
-Where's Oren?

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:35.802
[ Door opens ]

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:38.805 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:39.839
Oren.

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:41.941
-I've kept my side
of the bargain.

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.310
Now, where's the relic?

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.880
-Please welcome back to the
show Catherine Zeta-Jones!

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.883
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:50.883 --> 00:01:00.159 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:09.468 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:11.304
Welcome back, Catherine.

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.539
-It's always lovely to see you,
Seth.

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:15.542
-You're very villainous
in that clip.

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.343
-I'm a mean girl.
-Yes.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:18.578
Do you enjoy a little villainy?

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.580
-Oh, I so loved it.
-Yes.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.581
It seems it comes to you
very naturally.

00:01:22.581 --> 00:01:25.685
-Well, yeah.
No, it doesn't.

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:29.855
I'm actually a nice Welsh girl,
but I put that blond wig on.

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:31.858
-Yes, I have a photo, 'cause the
blonde --

00:01:31.858 --> 00:01:33.726
Was this --
Did you get to have a hand

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:34.927
in the choosing of the wig?

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:37.129
-I did, yeah.
I wanted something different.

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:41.134
After coming off Morticia,
I thought let's do blonde,

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:43.402
and I wanted to know
if blondes have more fun.

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:44.670
-And did you have a good time?

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.372
-I had a great time.
-That's wonderful.

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:49.109
This is a spinoff series
based on

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:50.876
the "National Treasure" films.
-Yes.

00:01:50.876 --> 00:01:53.780
-And it's obviously
much like those films --

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.915
a great deal about history,
about investigating.

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.250
Were you a good student
growing up?

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:01.020
-I was a conscientious student,

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.056
but I spent half my time
in the theater,

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:06.159
so I had to go back
and, like, play catch-up.

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:09.295
But history,
of all the subjects,

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:10.830
was literally my favorite.

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.766
And my kids are both --
my son's graduated.

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:16.935
He's just finished -- graduated
with history at college.

00:02:16.935 --> 00:02:18.004
-That's wonderful.
-And my daughter's doing it.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:20.906
So we come from
a history-loving family.

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:23.443
So this show
is right up my alley.

00:02:23.443 --> 00:02:25.944
-Were they fans of the original?

00:02:25.944 --> 00:02:27.113
Are they the age
where they watched

00:02:27.113 --> 00:02:28.047
the original
"National Treasure" films?

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:29.382
-Well, they were babes in arms

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.951
when the originals came out,
and I loved them.

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:35.020
When Jerry Bruckheimer called me
up to do part of it,

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.589
I was like, "Well,
who am I gonna play?"

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:39.992
I remember Nic Cage,
Harvey Keitel, Justin Bartha,

00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:42.228
but they told me there was this
new character.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:45.798
And I long-windedly
told my kids about,

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.333
"When you were babes in arms,

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:51.036
there was these two films,
and they were fabulous.

00:02:51.036 --> 00:02:52.771
It was all about history
and this treasure hunt."

00:02:52.771 --> 00:02:54.373
They went, "Whoa, whoa,
are you talking about

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:55.541
'National Treasure'?"

00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:57.042
And I went, "You know it?"

00:02:57.042 --> 00:02:59.311
They went like,
"Yes, we love it."

00:02:59.311 --> 00:03:01.047
So it was just great.

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.082
I didn't -- I didn't realize
that, you know,

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:06.052
they had such great legs,
that franchise.

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:08.655
-Yeah.
-So it lends itself

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:12.091
to a great 10-part
series on Disney+,

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:15.561
because unlike the film,
as great as they were,

00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:17.130
is that 90-minute capsule.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:21.100
We got time to really --
I'm going to say something.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:22.968
I'm not mean all the time.
-No.

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:27.740
-I mean, you do wonder why this
woman wants this relic so bad.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.442
What is the --
-Seems like you've fallen

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:31.010
in love with this villain
character you're playing.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.178
-I did.
-You're out here defending her.

00:03:33.178 --> 00:03:34.847
-But I played a few. Look.

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:38.251
People forget -- In "Chicago,"
I was a double murderess,

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:40.252
and in "Traffic"
I was a drug dealer

00:03:40.252 --> 00:03:41.954
who completely did the whole --

00:03:41.954 --> 00:03:44.357
-Yeah, why are we letting you
off the look?

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:47.059
-Yeah!
Why is everyone to surprised?

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:49.662
-Your son came with you
the premiere.

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:50.930
Do you feel like a cool mom

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:53.332
when you get your handsome son
to be on your arm?

00:03:53.332 --> 00:03:55.568
-I do, and we bought him
that suit in London.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:56.803
-Did you?
-Yeah.

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:58.705
It's his first kind of London --

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:01.240
He said, "You look like you're
out of the 'Dead Poets Society.'

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:02.642
Is that a good thing, Mum?

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:04.010
Is that a good thing?"
I went, "Yeah."

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:07.113
But you know what, he's --
he was in school for four years,

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:08.847
so he gets the chance now
to come along

00:04:08.847 --> 00:04:10.182
because Michael's working.

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:14.220
I just -- It's the gift
that keeps on giving, Seth.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.755
I don't know what to say.
-You and Michael Douglas,

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:17.690
22 years married,
congratulations.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:20.759
That's an accomplishment.
-I know.

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:23.963
Can you imagine 22 years?
-Yeah.

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:26.499
-We had -- Yeah,
and we have the same birthday.

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:28.901
-Oh, that's wonderful.
-We have like September 25th

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.636
is our same --
25 years difference.

00:04:30.636 --> 00:04:33.339
-Yeah, okay.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:36.375
Not the same birthday.
-Not the same day.

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:39.879
But -- And so we have
September 25th is our birthday

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:43.515
and then November 18th
is our anniversary.

00:04:43.515 --> 00:04:45.885
So we went off to Morocco.

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:48.788
-That's very --
-Fabulous, actually, yeah.

00:04:48.788 --> 00:04:51.423
-Do you -- Historically,
do your kids...

00:04:51.423 --> 00:04:54.093
Have you introduced them
to your work, you and Michael?

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:55.461
Are they fans?

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:57.029
Or is it weird for them
because you're their parents?

00:04:57.029 --> 00:04:59.265
-They've seen some.

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:01.767
And they say that they've seen
everything, but they haven't.

00:05:01.767 --> 00:05:03.703
I get it, you know?
And I'm okay with that.

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:05.471
I haven't seen everything
I've done either.

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:07.206
[ Laughter ]
-Do you know --

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:08.941
When you're making one, do you
ever think to yourself,

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:10.109
"I'm probably never
going to see this"?

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:12.945
-No, it's not like that.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:16.682
No!

00:05:16.682 --> 00:05:20.086
I actually -- I'm way too
critical and analytical.

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:22.387
And it's -- you know, I'm --

00:05:22.387 --> 00:05:24.189
-I agree. I don't love
watching myself either.

00:05:24.189 --> 00:05:27.193
-Every now and again something
comes on TV and I go,

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:29.328
"Oh, I think I'm -- I'm in that"
and I watch it.

00:05:29.328 --> 00:05:32.798
But my kids want to be actors,
even though they're --

00:05:32.798 --> 00:05:35.868
I was convinced they were going
to be history teachers.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.638
And so they love
the craft of acting,

00:05:38.638 --> 00:05:40.272
and they get our business,
you know.

00:05:40.272 --> 00:05:42.809
-Yeah.
-Which, my gosh,

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:44.677
this business
has been great to me.

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:47.146
I've had a really
wonderful life thus far.

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:49.048
-Well, there you go.
I have a lot more to ask you.

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:51.417
We'll be right back with more
from Catherine Zeta-Jones.

